# Byte-compared test data: a checkout must hand the tests the bytes the
# repository holds. `-text` turns off end-of-line conversion, which a Windows
# checkout otherwise applies (core.autocrlf): it turned a fixture's `\n` into
# `\r\n` and failed a byte comparison for a reason unrelated to the code under
# test (docs/09 P10-29). `-text`, not `eol=lf`: one fixture is CRLF as captured
# (tests/fixtures/guidde/subtitles-reference.vtt), and `eol=lf` would mark it
# as text and let the next add renormalize it to LF.
tests/fixtures/** -text
tests/golden/** -text
tests/parity/** -text
